# Deliciously Moist Chocolate Layer Cake

Based on [Sally’s Baking Addiction](https://sallysbakingaddiction.com/triple-chocolate-layer-cake/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Cake

- [ ] 1.75 cups (219g) [all-purpose flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup (62g) [unsweetened cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-cocoa-powder" }
- [ ] 1.75 cups (350g) [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" } (optional)
- [ ] 1/2 cup (120ml) [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }
- [ ] 2 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, room temperature
- [ ] 2 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 1 cup (240ml) [buttermilk]{ ing="buttermilk" }, room temperature
- [ ] 1 cup (240ml) freshly [brewed strong hot coffee]{ ing="brewed-strong-hot-coffee" }

### Buttercream Frosting

- [ ] 1.25 cups (282g) [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }, softened
- [ ] 3.5 cups (420g) [confectioners’ sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }
- [ ] 3/4 cup (62g) [unsweetened cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-cocoa-powder" }
- [ ] 3-5 Tbsps (45-75ml) [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }, room temperature
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] [Semi-sweet chocolate chips]{ ing="semi-sweet-chocolate-chips" } (optional, for decoration)

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350°F. Grease two 9-inch pans, line with parchment, and grease again for seamless release.
1. Whisk [flour]{ ing="all-purpose-flour" }, cocoa, [sugar]{ ing="confectioners-sugar" }, [baking soda]{ ing="baking-soda" }, [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [espresso powder]{ ing="espresso-powder" } together. Mix [oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }, [eggs]{ ing="egg" }, and vanilla on medium-high speed. Add [buttermilk]{ ing="buttermilk" }, then combine wet and dry ingredients with [hot coffee]{ ing="brewed-strong-hot-coffee" } until fully blended (batter is thin).
1. Divide batter between pans and bake 23-26 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean. Cool completely in pans.
1. Beat softened [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } until creamy (about 2 minutes). Add confectioners’ sugar, [cocoa powder]{ ing="unsweetened-cocoa-powder" }, 3 Tbsps [cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }, salt, and vanilla. Beat on low for 30 seconds, then high for 1 minute. Adjust consistency as needed.
1. Level cake tops with a serrated knife if domed. Place first layer on serving plate, frost top, add second layer, and frost top and sides.
1. Refrigerate uncovered for 30-60 minutes to set. Serve at room temperature or chilled.

## Notes

- Store covered in refrigerator for up to 5 days.
